<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/081402d32175> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving cars from rivals Google, Delphi in close call" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "269" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/081d40ff58c0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[268] The other vehicle in question was an Audi Q5 crossover fitted with self-driving equipment developed by Delphi Automotive." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "268" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1093776eadb8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google and Delphi self-driving cars in near miss" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5292" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/10e7fa3aa9ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Although Delphi is testing only two Audi prototypes, Google has had more than 20 Lexus vehicles equipped with its technology on California roads." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "274" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11825daad1de> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Robo-car wars: Delphi's near crash, prang, wallop with Google DENIED!" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "267" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/12b8b96bb10f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has driven more than a million miles in these vehicles since 2009 and had finally hit the streets of California this week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5288" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1fa6b4d892aa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5290] A car from Google's fleet reportedly cut off an Audi being tested by rival Delphi Automotive during a lane change." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2f8f257f999d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 of the main reasons behind Google’s commitment to driverless cars is their ability to avoid accidents and improve traffic safety." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "268" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/319721840999> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Absmeier was a passenger in a prototype Audi Q5 crossover vehicle equipped with lasers, radar, cameras and special computer software designed to enable the vehicle to drive itself, with a person at the wheel as a backup." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1973" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/31b75b2832ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi is back-pedaling after one of its executives told Reuters last week one of its self-driving vehicles had to take evasive maneuvers to avoid being side-swiped by an autonomous Google car." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "274" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/33de88a4cc1a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5288] The self-driving prototype cars involved in the incident were operated by Google and by Delphi Automotive." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5288" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3ed99b973454> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi, which recently drove a self-driving Audi across country, does most of its test drives near its autonomous driving lab." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "269" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4c0d5af1f674> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Driverless Car Maker Denies Claim of Near-Miss With Google Car" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "266" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d1b11c7c362> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving cars narrowly avoid California crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/601341b04593> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The self-driving prototype cars involved in the incident were operated by Google and by Delphi Automotive." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5288" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/61c118db6df5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google and Delphi’s self-driving cars have near miss" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5288" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e2871cebc3f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google has 23 self-driving Lexus RX450h crossovers on the road, and recently put nine prototypes of its own self-driving car design on the road as well.",
        "Google has 23 self-driving Lexus RX450h crossovers on the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "269" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/721b349e7548> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google and Delphi self-driving cars in near miss" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "270" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7cedba90075d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi Changes Story, Says Google Self-Driving Car Did Not Nearly Crash Into Audi" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "274" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7fc27f8f55a7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5292] In a showdown of self-driving cars a Google vehicle recently cut off a Delphi car attempting to switch roadway lanes, and came perilously close to crashing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5292" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/833b604b450d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Two rival self-driving cars have close call in California" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1973" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/87deb37ea5e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google's Driverless Car Almost Hit Delphi's Autonomous Vehicle, Report Says" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "268" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/99584ba51e3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Robo-car wars: Delphi's near crash, prang, wallop with Google DENIED!" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5286" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9e759b8fb6ee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi Automotive has contradicted a senior exec at the company by denying that one of its robo-cars had come close to being pranged by a Google self-driving vehicle." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5286" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/abd1bfad68bd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5290] A car from Google's fleet reportedly cut off an Audi being tested by rival Delphi Automotive during a lane change." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ae503434c547> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As the Delphi vehicle prepared to change lanes, a Google self-driving prototype - a Lexus RX400h crossover fitted with similar hardware and software - cut off the Audi, forcing it to abort the lane change, Absmeier said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1973" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b24b73aebc0c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The California Department of Motor Vehicles also says in all cases, the self-driving cars were not at fault." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5288" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d38c670dc3ef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In all cases, the self-driving prototype was not at fault, according to the California Department of Motor Vehicles and the companies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1973" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/edd7ff57e88f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 self-driving prototype cars, one operated by Google Inc and the other by Delphi Automotive Plc, had a close call on a Silicon Valley street earlier this week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1973" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f23c1512bd15> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving cars are allowed on streets and highways in California, but they are required to have a human driver sitting behind the steering wheel able to take over control of the car if there is a problem." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "269" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7bdc7fc837f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[270] Self-driving cars are allowed on streets and highways in California, but they're required to have a human sitting behind the steering wheel to take charge if there's a problem." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "270" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f83470a4a96a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1973] The incident occurred Tuesday on San Antonio Road in Palo Alto, said John Absmeier, director of Delphi’s Silicon Valley lab and global business director for the company’s automated driving program, who was a passenger in one of the cars." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1973" .

