<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e5c5b304be0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5290] 2 self-driving cars owned by Google and Delphi only just escaped a collision on Californian roads earlier this week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/62335a98e6d5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5290] Delphi's vehicle took \"appropriate action\" to avert an accident, company executive John Absmeier, who was in the car during the encounter, told Reuters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aba504b2727f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Self-driving cars are allowed on streets and highways in California, but they're required to have a human sitting behind the steering wheel to take charge if there's a problem." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "270" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e6a0f4832888> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Auto parts maker Delphi says that its experimental self-driving car was on a street in Silicon Valley earlier this week and was moving into another lane when an experimental self-driving car from Google cut it off by moving into the same lane.",
        "Auto parts maker Delphi says that its experimental self-driving car was on a street in Silicon Valley earlier this week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "269" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/37c3285c99e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a showdown of self-driving cars a Google vehicle recently cut off a Delphi car attempting to switch roadway lanes, and came perilously close to crashing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5292" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/607ec89960a0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "He said, according to the report, that Google's Lexus RX400h had cut off Delphi's Audi Q5 SUV – the car Absmeier was travelling in as a passenger on San Atonia Road in Palo Alto, California at the time of the incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5286" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eb4a9fcba16c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a showdown of self-driving cars a Google vehicle recently cut off a Delphi car attempting to switch roadway lanes, and came perilously close to crashing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "270" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fb5a29a63737> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After a report that a Delphi driverless car and a Google driverless car came close to a traffic incident on a road in Palo Alto, Calif., Delphi has issued a statement that “the vehicles didn’t even come close to each other.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "266" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/06cfc5e44fc1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google's Chris Urmson, director for the firm's driverless cars project, boasted of the vehicles' safety record in a blog post last month." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/416a074a3656> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The other vehicle in question was an Audi Q5 crossover fitted with self-driving equipment developed by Delphi Automotive." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "268" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/571fe226ef7e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi's vehicle took \"appropriate action\" to avert an accident, company executive John Absmeier, who was in the car during the encounter, told Reuters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5290" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9bc86cee0884> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Absmeier had apparently told Reuters, which stands by its original story, that the prototype cars had been involved in a near miss." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5286" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f038a3510ba9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The firm told Reuters on Friday that the news wire's earlier report – which earlier this week had quoted John Absmeier, Delphi's Silicon Valley lab director, describing a close call with Google's car – was wrong." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5286" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/05dae7779596> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As reported by Reuters, one of Google’s driverless cars nearly collided with another car while driving in Silicon Valley." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "268" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8de59b667eb1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Although Delphi executive John Absmeier — who was in the self-driving Audi (run by Delphi software) at the time of the incident — originally told Reuters the Delphi car “took appropriate action” to avoid being hit by a Google-operated self-driving Lexus, the company is now saying “the vehicles didn’t even come close to each other.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "274" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c49bfaa23209> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi disclosed the incident to a Reuters reporter earlier this week and confirmed it to CNNMoney Friday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "269" .

